mod main;

// output:
// hello, world
// 4631107791820423168
// 42

/*
 * The first program the bootstrap compiler runs (doc/codegen.md 13.1): a
 * main that prints a text and a number through the library's println.
 *
 * The long number is what the C++-built program prints too: println of a
 * number goes to the library's print_num, whose asm prints the decimal's
 * bits with `put` (an integer print), so 42.0 comes out as 4631107791820423168.
 * The oracle is the C++-built program, so that is the right output here.
 * show() (tests/codegen/print.sharp) prints the integer itself.
 */
def main() {
    println("hello, world");
    n : _int64 = 6 * 7;
    println(n);
    show(n);
}
